# The wolf pack in the narrows of the Old Svalich Road. NPC mists_wolves blocks the road until this resolves.
# Talking them down sets mists_wolves_cowed; a fight is the mists_wolves encounter (3 wolves, 150 XP, level 1).
# Speak with Animals asks them what they want: the master sent them to look (and there's an old man in the fog).

~ start
Narrator: A grey wolf stands square in the narrows, head low, while more shapes wait in the fog beyond it and something shifts in the trees behind you. None of them growl; they are waiting to see what you do.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Good dog. Nice dog. Apricot? No? No. Very sensible.
if not name:kip_smudgewick
  interject species:halfling: Just so everyone knows, I'm the bite-sized one.
endif
-> choose

~ choose
* [Intimidation DC 13] Stand tall and shout them off the road. If they don't give way, they attack. -> cowed_shout | attack
* [Animal Handling DC 12] Eyes down, move slowly, walk through. Startle them and they attack. -> cowed_gentle | attack
* [if flag.mists_read_the_pack] [Insight DC 10] They're sentries, not hunters: nod to them and walk on. Misjudge them and they attack. -> cowed_sentries | attack
* [Wizard] [Arcana DC 12] Scatter them with harmless light and thunder. If they don't scare, they attack. -> cowed_magic | attack
* [if spell:speak_with_animals] Ask the lead wolf what they want. -> spoken
* [if not spell:speak_with_animals] [knows:speak_with_animals] (Cast Speak with Animals, and ask the lead wolf what they want.) -> speak_cast
* Draw steel and kill the leader before it calls the rest. -> fight_first
* Wait for them to leave. -> wait

~ wait
Narrator: You wait, and the wolves wait longer. When you finally look up, every one of them is still looking at you.
interject name:ratatoille: Non, they are not leaving. They hold a line, like sentries at a gate. Someone has drilled them.
-> choose

~ speak_cast
cast speak_with_animals
if check.last
-> spoken
endif
-> choose

# Speak with Animals (2024 PHB): the master's wolves answer, and let the party by.
~ spoken
set mists_read_the_pack
Narrator: The lead wolf listens with its head on one side. Its answer comes as much in smell and the set of its ears as in words, and it is very simple.
Narrator: "The master wants to look at you. Not eat. Look. Walk on to the houses. He sees everything that comes out of the white, and he will see you soon."
if not flag.ilarion_met
Narrator: "There is an old one in the white, back where you came out, who sits on a stone and asks the trees what day it is. We don't eat him. The master says not yet."
endif
Narrator: It steps aside like a doorman, and the pack goes into the fog to tell someone what it saw.
approve thistle +2: You asked the master's wolves what they wanted, in their own tongue
-> resolved

~ cowed_shout
Narrator: {name}'s voice cracks across the narrows like a whip. The lead wolf holds its ground for one long breath, then turns and trots into the fog, and the pack goes with it, unhurried, as if it had somewhere to report.
-> resolved

~ cowed_gentle
Narrator: {name} walks into the narrows with eyes lowered and hands open. The lead wolf sniffs once, steps aside like a doorman, and the pack melts into the trees.
approve thistle +2: You walked through the wolves with your eyes down, the way you'd pass a strange dog
-> resolved

~ cowed_sentries
Narrator: {name} meets the lead wolf's eyes and nods, the way you nod to a guard at a gate. It considers this, then lets you pass, and the fog fills up with wolves going somewhere to tell someone.
-> resolved

~ cowed_magic
Narrator: Light flares white and a clap of thunder rolls down the road. The wolves scatter into the fog, and from somewhere farther off, a single long howl answers, as if passing on the news.
-> resolved

~ resolved
set mists_wolves_resolved
set mists_wolves_cowed
quest into_the_mists the_pack
interject name:thistle: Wasn't fear. They were sent off. Somebody's whistling for them.
if not name:thistle
  interject class:cleric: Wolves don't keep ranks. Not on their own.
endif
-> END

~ attack
Narrator: The lead wolf's lips peel back from its teeth. Behind you, in the trees, something answers it.
set mists_wolves_resolved
quest into_the_mists the_pack
combat mists_wolves

~ fight_first
Narrator: Steel clears leather. The wolves were waiting for exactly that.
set mists_wolves_resolved
quest into_the_mists the_pack
combat mists_wolves
